---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Start Here">
	<div class="container docs-container">
		<div class="doc-content">
			<h1 class="serif">Start Here</h1>
			<p class="lede">Provide the onboarding flow for an operator's first session.</p>
			
			<div class="section-head">
				<h2 class="serif">1. Prepare your environment</h2>
			</div>
			<p>You need three things to run the Autonomous Duck Deployment Framework:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>A capable LLM (Claude, ChatGPT, etc.)</li>
				<li>A terminal</li>
				<li>A markdown editor</li>
			</ul>

			<div class="section-head">
				<h2 class="serif">2. Download the Starter Kit</h2>
			</div>
			<p>Download the blank starter kit from the <a href="/Autonomous-Duck-Development-Framework/downloads" style="text-decoration: underline;">Downloads page</a>. Extract it into your project directory. This provides the canonical file structure.</p>

			<div class="section-head">
				<h2 class="serif">3. Initialize the Project Brain</h2>
			</div>
			<p>Open <code>STATE.md</code>, <code>DOMAIN.md</code>, and <code>DECISIONS.md</code>. Fill in the placeholder details for your project. The files are the project — these definitions will guide every AI session moving forward.</p>

			<div class="section-head">
				<h2 class="serif">4. Run your first session</h2>
			</div>
			<p>Copy the first-session prompt from the prompt catalog, load the required files, and declare the mode. You are now operating within ADDF.</p>
			
			<div class="cta-area">
				<a href="/Autonomous-Duck-Development-Framework/downloads" class="btn btn-primary">Go to Downloads →</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.docs-container {
		padding: var(--space-10) var(--space-5);
		max-width: 720px;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.lede {
		font-size: 20px;
		color: var(--ink-soft);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
	}

	.section-head {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
		padding-bottom: var(--space-3);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
		margin-top: var(--space-8);
	}

	p {
		margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
	}

	ul {
		padding-left: var(--space-5);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
	}

	li {
		margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
	}

	code {
		font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
		font-size: 0.92em;
		background-color: rgba(20,17,13,0.06);
		padding: 2px 4px;
		border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
	}

	.cta-area {
		margin-top: var(--space-8);
	}
</style>
